{
  "annotations": {
    "list": [
      {
        "builtIn": 1,
        "datasource": "-- Grafana --",
        "enable": true,
        "hide": true,
        "iconColor": "rgba(0, 211, 255, 1)",
        "name": "Annotations & Alerts",
        "type": "dashboard"
      },
      {
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "prometheus"
        },
        "enable": true,
        "hide": false,
        "iconColor": "rgba(242, 73, 92, 0.5)",
        "name": "No available pods",
        "expr": "(kube_deployment_spec_replicas{deployment=~\"$app\"} > 0) and on (namespace, deployment) (kube_deployment_status_replicas_available == 0) and on (deployment) label_replace(group by (app) (last_over_time(http_server_request_duration_seconds_count[1h])), \"deployment\", \"$1\", \"app\", \"(.*)\")",
        "step": "15s",
        "titleFormat": "No available pods",
        "textFormat": "{{namespace}}/{{deployment}}: no pod is Ready to serve",
        "tagKeys": "namespace,deployment",
        "useValueForTime": false
      }
    ]
  },
  "description": "Server-side application request metrics alongside the k6 load generator's client-side view.",
  "editable": true,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "links": [],
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How to read this dashboard",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Server-side** panels (`http_server_request_duration_seconds_count`) count what the app actually handled; **client-side** panels (`k6_*`) count what the load generator sent and got back. Below the first row, the left column is the server's view and the right column is k6's view of the same question. A gap between them is the interesting signal: requests dropped at the ingress, rejected by a full queue, or lost to pod restarts never reach the app's counters.\n\nGenerate load with `labctl traffic start --profile steady --rps 25`. The `k6_*` series only appear while a run is in flight."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Request rate by app (server-side)",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [],
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "stacking": {
              "group": "A",
              "mode": "none"
            }
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "reqps"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (app) (rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_count[1m])) or 0 * group by (app) (last_over_time(http_server_request_duration_seconds_count[1h]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{app}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "format": "time_series"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Every route is metered by one middleware, so this moves for any traffic the app serves. An app seen in the last hour that handles nothing, because no pod is serving, reads 0 rather than disappearing."
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Request rate by route",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 4
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [],
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "stacking": {
              "group": "A",
              "mode": "none"
            }
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "reqps"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (app, http_route) (rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_count{app=~\"$app\"}[1m])) or 0 * group by (app, http_route) (last_over_time(http_server_request_duration_seconds_count{app=~\"$app\"}[1h]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{app}} {{http_route}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "format": "time_series"
        }
      ],
      "description": "The route label is normalised to known routes plus 'other', so cardinality stays bounded. A route seen in the last hour reads 0 while nothing is served on it."
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Latency percentiles (server-side)",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 28
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [],
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "stacking": {
              "group": "A",
              "mode": "none"
            }
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "s"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.50, sum by (le, app) (rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_bucket{app=~\"$app\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p50 {{app}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "format": "time_series"
        },
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le, app) (rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_bucket{app=~\"$app\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p95 {{app}}",
          "refId": "B",
          "format": "time_series"
        },
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le, app) (rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_bucket{app=~\"$app\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p99 {{app}}",
          "refId": "C",
          "format": "time_series"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Quantiles are estimated from histogram buckets, and the first bucket ends at 5ms. Below that Grafana can only interpolate, so a fast app reads p50 2.5ms, p95 4.75ms and p99 4.95ms: treat those values as \"under 5ms\"."
    },
    {
