        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (app) (rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_count{app=~\"$app\", http_response_status_code=~\"5..\"}[1m])) or 0 * group by (app) (last_over_time(http_server_request_duration_seconds_count{app=~\"$app\"}[1h]))",
          "legendFormat": "5xx {{app}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "format": "time_series"
        }
      ],
      "description": "5xx responses per second the app itself returned. It also reads 0 during a total outage: an app that is not running returns nothing, so read an outage from k6 failed request rate and Responses by outcome (k6 client)."
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Offered vs served: k6 offered vs app handled",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 36
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [],
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "stacking": {
              "group": "A",
              "mode": "none"
            }
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "reqps"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "((sum(rate(k6_http_reqs_total{url=~\"https?://$app\\\\..*\"}[1m])) or vector(0)) + (sum(rate(k6_dropped_iterations_total[1m])) or vector(0))) and on () (count(last_over_time(k6_http_reqs_total{url=~\"https?://$app\\\\..*\"}[5m])) > 0)",
          "legendFormat": "k6 offered (client)",
          "refId": "A",
          "format": "time_series"
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_count{app=~\"$app\"}[1m])) or vector(0)",
          "legendFormat": "handled by the app (server)",
          "refId": "B",
          "format": "time_series"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Two lines that should overlap when only k6 is loading the selected apps. k6 offered is every request the run was asked to send: the ones it sent plus the ones it dropped because every virtual user was still waiting on an earlier request. The apps count what they handled, which also includes kubelet probes and any traffic that did not come from k6. A persistent gap beyond that means requests are lost before reaching the app. When no pod is serving at all, the app line drops to zero while the offered line stays at the configured rate."
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "k6 client-observed latency",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 28
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [],
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "stacking": {
              "group": "A",
              "mode": "none"
            }
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "s"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "label_replace(label_replace(max by (url) (k6_http_req_duration_p95{url=~\"https?://$app\\\\..*\"} and on (url, status) (rate(k6_http_reqs_total{url=~\"https?://$app\\\\..*\", status!=\"0\"}[1m]) > 0)), \"app\", \"$1\", \"url\", \"https?://([^.]+)\\\\..*\"), \"route\", \"$1\", \"url\", \"https?://[^/]+(/.*)\")",
          "legendFormat": "p95 {{app}} {{route}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "format": "time_series"
        },
        {
          "expr": "label_replace(label_replace(max by (url) (k6_http_req_duration_p99{url=~\"https?://$app\\\\..*\"} and on (url, status) (rate(k6_http_reqs_total{url=~\"https?://$app\\\\..*\", status!=\"0\"}[1m]) > 0)), \"app\", \"$1\", \"url\", \"https?://([^.]+)\\\\..*\"), \"route\", \"$1\", \"url\", \"https?://[^/]+(/.*)\")",
          "legendFormat": "p99 {{app}} {{route}}",
          "refId": "B",
          "format": "time_series"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Latency as the k6 client measured it, per route it hit. The k6 panels follow the App selector through the URL each request was sent to. Each status's latency is drawn only while k6 is still getting that status back, so a burst of errors does not linger after it ends; a request that got no response has no latency, so a total outage is a gap."
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "k6 failed request rate",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 20
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [],
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "stacking": {
              "group": "A",
              "mode": "none"
            }
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "percentunit"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "label_replace(label_replace((sum by (url) (rate(k6_http_reqs_total{url=~\"https?://$app\\\\..*\",expected_response=\"false\"}[1m])) or 0 * sum by (url) (rate(k6_http_reqs_total{url=~\"https?://$app\\\\..*\"}[1m]))) / sum by (url) (rate(k6_http_reqs_total{url=~\"https?://$app\\\\..*\"}[1m])), \"app\", \"$1\", \"url\", \"https?://([^.]+)\\\\..*\"), \"route\", \"$1\", \"url\", \"https?://[^/]+(/.*)\")",
          "legendFormat": "{{app}} {{route}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "format": "time_series"
        }
      ],
      "description": "The share of requests k6 sent in the last minute that did not get the response it expected, per route. Unlike the server-side error panel it includes requests that never reached the app."
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Responses by outcome (k6 client)",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 12
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [],
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "bars",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 80,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "stacking": {
              "group": "A",
              "mode": "normal"
            }
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "reqps"
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byRegexp",
              "options": ".* 2[0-9][0-9]$"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "green"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byRegexp",
              "options": ".* 3[0-9][0-9]$"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "blue"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byRegexp",
              "options": ".* 4[0-9][0-9]$"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "orange"
